/*
 * WRO Future Engineers 2026 - OPEN CHALLENGE (no traffic signs)
 * Board: Arduino Mega 2560
 * Gyro:  HW-290 module (MPU6050 on I2C: SDA=20, SCL=21 on Mega)
 * Steering: hobby SERVO on pin 4 (replaces the old DC-motor steering)
 *
 * Hardware (matches your pin list):
 *   Steering servo:    signal pin 4
 *   Driving motor:     IN3(32), IN4(33), power ENB(3)
 *   Front ultrasonic:  trig 38, echo 39
 *   Right ultrasonic:  trig 40, echo 41
 *   Left  ultrasonic:  trig 42, echo 43
 *   Start button:      pin 5 -> GND (uses INPUT_PULLUP)  [required by rules 9.10/9.11]
 *
 *   NOTE: the servo needs its own 5-6V supply (from your regulator/BEC),
 *   not the Arduino 5V pin, and share GND with the Arduino. IN1/IN2/ENA
 *   are no longer used since the DC steering motor and L298N channel A
 *   were replaced by the servo.
 *
 * Logic:
 *   1. Wait for start button.
 *   2. Drive straight for 1s (gyro holds heading), then keep driving straight.
 *      Steering = gyro heading hold + gentle wall centering from the side
 *      sensors + a slow auto-trim that learns the car's steering bias.
 *   3. Corner detection: the WRO corridor is never wider than ~100cm, so a
 *      side sensor reading past SIDE_OPEN_CM (130cm) can ONLY mean the inner
 *      wall ended = corner opened on that side. Turn toward it. Must hold for
 *      2 consecutive reads (rejects one-off bad echoes). The first corner
 *      also fixes the driving direction for the whole run.
 *   4. Each corner: target heading changes by 90 deg, gyro turns us there.
 *      Before the next corner can count, the watched side must first read
 *      CLOSED again (re-arm) and a time cooldown must pass.
 *   5. Front wall < 70cm is the second corner cue (narrow sections open the
 *      side very late). At the FIRST corner with no side open, turn toward
 *      the CLOSER side - the ring always bends toward its center.
 *   6. If TURNING makes no progress for 2.5s (nose pinned on a wall), back
 *      up briefly and resume the turn.
 *   7. Count corners. 12 corners = 3 laps. Then drive into the start section
 *      until the far wall reads FINISH_FRONT_CM (mid-section) and stop
 *      (rule 9.24.2: must stop autonomously).
 *
 * Debugging: telemetry is recorded to EEPROM during every run and replayed
 * as CSV over serial at boot (see EEPROM FLIGHT RECORDER below).
 */

